<title>USA: Raytheon gets $566.8 mln defense contract.</title>
<headline>Raytheon gets $566.8 mln defense contract.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Demilitarization Co, a division of Raytheon Corp, has received a $566.8 million multi-year U.S. defense contract for operation and subsequent closure of the Umatilla Chemical Agent Disposal Facility, the Army said.</p>
<p>Work will be done in Hermiston, Oregon, and is expected to be completed by Feb. 16, 2006, according to the Army.</p>
</text>
